#{[17592186553192 #edb/ref 1080 "3{x}^{2}+xy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a031cdff-6a41-52e9-aeab-5a6e16f24cf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553300 #edb/ref 1080 "4({x}^{2}-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553300 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553300 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d69014c4-c493-5bef-9f1c-7c17c3e7aba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553310 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{2}(-{y}^{4}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553310 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553310 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de294dc0-1a3f-5566-a574-17c08dcba154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553372 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}({y}^{4}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553372 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553372 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fe53b468-ca8f-540a-b5a9-6cfac0008d06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553436 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7efa0a56-60d9-584e-8007-e5d380ed9d48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553440 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8bc52748-240b-5997-9e36-b5b9d7c36232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127225" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1071 "According to the flux form of Green's theorem, the flux of the vector field \n$F(x,y)=⟨{x}^{3}+{y}^{2},\\,{x}^{2}y⟩$\nacross the triangle $C$ with vertices $(1,0),(0,2),$ and $(-1,2)$ can be represented as\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise, $n$ is the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C,$ and $D$ is the region bounded by $C.$ Calculate the function $f(x,y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "30b095cd-424c-553d-bb7d-82a5c5e826eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553511 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/84/848dfedddea9803dcf39b4624f2966b63f080920ed19b875dc691e8fe9d3b038.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{3}+{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}y.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the flux form of Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3{x}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127230" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the rectangle $C$ with vertices $(-1,0),(-1,-2),(3,-2),$ and $(3,0),$ traversed counterclockwise. Using the flux form of Green's theorem, express the flux of the vector field\n$F(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{6}\\,i-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}\\,j$\nthrough $C$ as a repeated integral." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5c8c9fb-a926-5fe7-b24d-28d3915fc2cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553576 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e1e4386f3cc75afb63823d74daa27b517e8e47d51fa08c5c9e5bf3ca6f3ca88c.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{6}$ and $Q(x,y)=-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{6},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-3{y}^{2}{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,-2\\le y\\le 0\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{6}-3{y}^{2}{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}({y}^{4}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553593 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04aa14d7-0210-5ec0-be65-62b34371b542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553602 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553602 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "17d9afa8-29a6-5cbe-a046-611ce72a4164" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553602 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553639 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553639 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "82ed2013-6159-51b4-a051-12e14d7b61bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553639 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553662 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553662 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0749924-f94a-5554-9f93-ea7596b1d1db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553662 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553687 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ffe0a3c1-5d07-5ea1-84fe-9437d4f004d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553687 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541081 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
